    "text": "To determine the total cost of Tom's deck, we need to calculate the cost of each type of card and then sum these costs.\n\n1. Calculate the cost of the rare cards:\n   - Tom has 19 rare cards.\n   - Each rare card costs $1.\n   - Therefore, the total cost for the rare cards is \\(19 \\times 1 = 19\\) dollars.\n\n2. Calculate the cost of the uncommon cards:\n   - Tom has 11 uncommon cards.\n   - Each uncommon card costs $0.50.\n   - Therefore, the total cost for the uncommon cards is \\(11 \\times 0.50 = 5.50\\) dollars.\n\n3. Calculate the cost of the common cards:\n   - Tom has 30 common cards.\n   - Each common card costs $0.25.\n   - Therefore, the total cost for the common cards is \\(30 \\times 0.25 = 7.50\\) dollars.\n\n4. Sum the costs of all the cards to find the total cost of the deck:\n   - The total cost is \\(19 + 5.50 + 7.50 = 32\\) dollars.\n\nThus, the total cost of Tom's deck is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
